StructuralRule.Notes:
express-graphql

Flags when graphqlHTTP invoked without disabling introspection. The standard method of
disabling introspection is by configuring the 'NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule'
validation rule when creating a GraphQL endpoint via graphqlHTTP().

OK: object passed to graphqlHTTP with validation rule set
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP({
    ...
    validationRules: [NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule]
}));

OK: lambda passed to graphqlHTTP returning object with validation rule set
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP((request) => {
    return {
        ...
        validationRules: [NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule]
    };
}));

NOT OK: validationRules not set
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP({
    schema
}));

NOT OK: NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule not included
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP({
    ...
   validationRules: [AuthenticationValidationRule]
}));

StructuralRule.Predicate:
FunctionCall fc:
    fc.possibleTargets contains [Function: name == "graphqlHTTP"]
    and fc.enclosingFunction is [Function:
        contains [FunctionCall:
            /* check if graphqlHTTP is argument of app.use() */
            possibleTargets contains [Function: name == "use"]
            and instance is [Expression inst:
                possibleHeapPaths contains [String str:
                    str matches "express(\.express|\.exports)?"
                ]
                /* for NodeGoat and similar projects. Bug 54435 */
                or inst is [Location: name == "app"]
            ]
            and arguments contains fc
        ]
    ]
    /* case 1: object passed as argument to graphqlHTTP() */
    and not fc.arguments[0] is [Expression:
        possibleTypes contains [Type:
            definition.fields contains [Field f1:
                f1.name == "validationRules"
                and fc.enclosingFunction contains [AssignmentStatement:
                    lhs is [FieldAccess:
                        field is f1
                    ]
                    and rhs is [VariableAccess va1:
                        fc.enclosingFunction contains [AssignmentStatement:
                            rhs is [VariableAccess:
                                name == "NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule"
                                and possibleTypes contains [Type:
                                    definition.name matches "NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule.*"
                                ]
                            ]
                            and lhs is [VariableAccess: is va1]
                        ]
                    ]
                ]
            ]
        ]
    ]
    /* case 2: lambda passed as argument to graphqlHTTP() */
    and not fc.arguments[0] is [Expression: 
        possibleFunctionTargets contains [Function lambda:
            returnSlot is [Slot: 
                type is [Type: 
                    definition.fields contains [Field f2:
                        f2.name == "validationRules"
                        and lambda contains [AssignmentStatement:
                            lhs is [FieldAccess:
                                field is f2
                            ]
                            and rhs is [VariableAccess va2:
                                fc.enclosingFunction contains [AssignmentStatement:
                                    rhs is [VariableAccess:
                                        name == "NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule"
                                        and possibleTypes contains [Type:
                                            definition.name matches "NoSchemaIntrospectionCustomRule.*"
                                        ]
                                    ]
                                    and lhs is [VariableAccess: is va2]
                                ]
                            ]
                        ]
                    ]
                ]
            ]
        ]
    ]

StructuralRule.Notes:
express-graphql

Flags when graphqlHTTP invoked without disabling GraphiQL. GraphiQL is disabled
by setting the "graphiql" field to false when creating a GraphQL endpoint by 
invoking graphiqlHTTP().

OK: object passed to graphqlHTTP with 'graphiql: false'
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP({
    ...
    graphiql: false
}));

OK: lambda passed to graphqlHTTP returning object with 'graphiql: false'
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP((request) => {
    return {
        ...
        graphiql: false
    };
}));

NOT OK: 'graphiql: false' missing
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP({
    schema
}));

NOT OK: graphiql explicitly enabled
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP({
    ...
    graphiql: true
}));

NOT OK: graphiql not disabled; config options provided
app.use('/graphiql', graphqlHTTP((request) => {
    return {
        ...
        graphiql: {
            defaultQuery: config.defaultQuery
        }
    };
}));

