CharacterizationRule.Notes:
Handlebars logging is of the form:
Handlebars.logger.log(level, ...message) Handlebars.log(level, ...message) or in a builtin helper:
{{log message level="info"}}

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function:
        name == "log"
        and (
            enclosingClass.name == "Logger"
            or fc.instance is [FieldAccess: 
                field is [Field: 
                    name == "logger"
                    and namespace.name == "Handlebars"
                ]
            ]
            or namespace.name == "Handlebars"
        )
    ]
    and fc.arguments contains [Expression arg: 
        not arg is fc.arguments[0]
    ]

CharacterizationRule.Notes:
Handlebars logging is of the form:
Handlebars.logger.log(level, ...message) Handlebars.log(level, ...message) or in a builtin helper:
{{log message level="info"}}

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function:
        name == "log"
        and (
            enclosingClass.name == "Logger"
            or fc.instance is [FieldAccess: 
                field is [Field: 
                    name == "logger"
                    and namespace.name == "Handlebars"
                ]
            ]
            or namespace.name == "Handlebars"
        )
    ]
    and fc.arguments contains [Expression arg: 
        not arg is fc.arguments[0]
    ]

FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function:
        name == "log"
        and (
            enclosingClass.name == "Logger"
            or fc.instance is [FieldAccess: 
                field is [Field: 
                    name == "logger"
                    and namespace.name == "Handlebars"
                ]
            ]
            or namespace.name == "Handlebars"
        )
    ]
    and fc.arguments[0] is [Expression e: 
        (
            /* check for DEBUG mode in 3.x */
            e is [FieldAccess fa: 
                fa.field.name == "DEBUG"
                /* 
                * honestly I can't be bothered to go about testing types
                * when this is only possible with really old versions of the library
                * so I'll just check the instance name to save time.
                */ 
                and fa.instance is [FieldAccess: field.name == "logger"
                    and instance is [Location: name == "Handlebars"]
                ]
            ]
        )
        /* constantValue for 0 or 'debug' debug logging */
        or e.constantValue == 0
        or e.constantValue == "debug"
    ]
    and fc.arguments contains [Expression arg: 
        not arg is fc.arguments[0]
    ]

FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function:
        name == "log"
