CharacterizationRule.Notes:
app.route('/')
  .get(function(req, res, next){
    //do something bad
  })
  .post(function(req, res, next){
    //do something bad
  });
Added `p.type.definition is [Class: name != "Request"]` to avoid duplication with 8C7F3218

app.route('/')
  .get(function(req, res, next){
    //do something bad
  })
  .post(function(req, res, next){
    //do something bad
  });

For case:

app.get('/', function(req, res){
    res.render('index.myExtension', {header: req.param('header') }, function(err, html){
        res.end(html);
    });
}

app.engine('myExtension', function(path, options, callback){
    options.header = options.header || "Hello World";
    callback(null, "<html><head></head><body><h1>" + options.header + "</h1></body></html>"); //possible XSS
}

Remove "app" conditions when bug 54435 fixed

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
FunctionCall fc: possibleTargets contains [Function:
    name == "engine"
]
and instance is [Expression inst: possibleHeapPaths contains [String str:
    str matches "express(\.express|\.exports)?"]
    /* for NodeGoat and similar projects. Bug 54435 */
    or inst is [Location: name == "app"]
]
and fc.arguments[1] is [Expression:
    possibleFunctionTargets contains [Function cb:
        contains [FunctionCall:
            possibleTargets contains [Function f:
                /* calls callback (arg2 of function) */
                cb.parameters[2] is [Variable:
                    name == f.name
                ]
            ]
            /* html sent to callback is changed by user */
            and arguments[1] is [Expression e: ]
        ]
    ]
]

