CharacterizationRule.Notes:
res.render(path, {variable_name: user_input}, function(err, html){
    res.send(html);
});

the locals/options object is optional, so lambda can be at arg1 or arg2.
If information goes into arg1, it goes into HTML.
This is only really useful for PV/SIL, but we don't have conditional args, and don't think we can add XSS validation taint on the arguments.
That being said, the 'err' parameter shouldn't be tainted (as long as the html successfully renders, this should be null), so I'm going to just set this to passing 'this', to stop incorrect tainting of err. A separate system info entrypoint is made for this.

