CharacterizationRule.Notes:
app = express();

app.get('/', function(req, res){
    var header = req.get('header_name'); //source
    // do something bad
})

or

app.route('/')
    .get(function(req, res){
    var header = req.get('header_name'); //source
    // do something bad
    });

Ideally would set type for "req" here but not possible at the moment, so need to find a workaround.

Also similar for express.Router().get(), etc.

Remove "app" conditions when bug 54435 fixed

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
FunctionCall fc: possibleTargets contains [Function: name matches "get|param|header"]
    /* can't uses reachedBy as need access to fc, so will check a couple of levels deep */
    and enclosingFunction is [Function lambda:
        parameters[0] is [Variable p:
            fc.instance is [VariableAccess: variable is p]
            /* what usually happens is the parameter is assigned to a field of the same name */
            /* this also means we can't use a variable's "uses" check, as this doesn't exist on fields */
            or fc.instance is [Location: name == p.name]
        ]
        and (
            callers contains [Function: contains [FunctionCall:
                /* check if function we're in was a lambda called by app.get(), etc */
                possibleTargets contains [Function: name matches "get|post|put|all|delete|checkout|copy|head|lock|merge|mkactivity|mkcol|move|m-search|notify|options|patch|purge|report|search|subscribe|trace|unlock|unsubscribe|use|param"]
                and instance is [Expression inst: possibleHeapPaths contains [String str:
                    str matches "(express|window)\.Router|express(\.express|\.exports)?"]
                    /* for NodeGoat and similar projects. Bug 54435 */
                    or inst is [Location: name == "app"]
                ]
                and arguments contains [Expression: possibleFunctionTargets contains lambda]
            ]]
            /* or if we're inside a lambda that was called from a function that was called by app.get()
            (so checking for a level of nesting) */
            or callers contains [Function: callers contains [Function: contains [FunctionCall:
                possibleTargets contains [Function: name matches "get|post|put|all|delete|checkout|copy|head|lock|merge|mkactivity|mkcol|move|m-search|notify|options|patch|purge|report|search|subscribe|trace|unlock|unsubscribe|use|param"]
                and instance is [Expression inst2: possibleHeapPaths contains [String str2:
                    str2 matches "(express|window)\.Router|express(\.express|\.exports)?"]
                    /* for NodeGoat and similar projects. Bug 54435 */
                    or inst2 is [Location: name == "app"]
                ]
                and arguments contains [Expression: possibleFunctionTargets contains lambda]
            ]]]
            or callers contains [Function: contains [FunctionCall:
                /* check if function we're in was a lambda called by app.route.get(), etc */
                possibleTargets contains [Function: name matches "get|post|put|all|delete|checkout|copy|head|lock|merge|mkactivity|mkcol|move|m-search|notify|options|patch|purge|report|search|subscribe|trace|unlock|unsubscribe|use|param"
                ]
                and instance.possibleHeapPaths contains [String str3:
                    str3 matches "(express|window)\.Router|[A-z]+\.route|window\.(get|post|put|all|delete|checkout|copy|head|lock|merge|mkactivity|mkcol|move|m-search|notify|options|patch|purge|report|search|subscribe|trace|unlock|unsubscribe)"
                ]
                and arguments contains [Expression: possibleFunctionTargets contains lambda]
            ]]
            /* or if we're inside a lambda that was called from a function that was called by app.route().get()
            (so checking for a level of nesting) */
            or callers contains [Function: callers contains [Function: contains [FunctionCall:
                possibleTargets contains [Function: name matches "get|post|put|all|delete|checkout|copy|head|lock|merge|mkactivity|mkcol|move|m-search|notify|options|patch|purge|report|search|subscribe|trace|unlock|unsubscribe|use|param"
                ]
                and instance.possibleHeapPaths contains [String str4:
                    str4 matches "(express|window)\.Router|[A-z]+\.route|window\.(get|post|put|all|delete|checkout|copy|head|lock|merge|mkactivity|mkcol|move|m-search|notify|options|patch|purge|report|search|subscribe|trace|unlock|unsubscribe)"
                ]
                and arguments contains [Expression: possibleFunctionTargets contains lambda]
            ]]]
        )
    ]

CharacterizationRule.Notes:
app = express();

app.get('/', function(req, res){
    var header = req.get('header_name'); //source
    // do something bad
})

or

app.route('/')
  .get(function(req, res){
    var header = req.get('header_name'); //source
    // do something bad
  });

Ideally would set type for "req" here but not possible at the moment, so need to find a workaround.

Also similar for express.Router().get(), etc.

Remove "app" conditions when bug 54435 fixed

